{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019HCEivhoASEyWSisjmXSqL","type":"tool_result","content":"=== superlative misconception claims ===\n338:- **A is wrong**, and it is the single most common misconception in this chapter: an image bundles application and system libraries, not a kernel [source: k8s-docs-containers-2026-08-23].\n348:- **A is wrong** for exactly that reason. This is the prior most readers arrive with.\n539:- **B is wrong**, and it is the most tempting distractor. The kubelet *ensures* that the containers described in PodSpecs are running and healthy [source: k8s-docs-cluster-architecture-2026-08-23]. It is the component that wants them to exist, not the one that creates them. It reaches a runtime across the CRI to do that.\n543:- **A is wrong**, and this is the most common misconception about the OCI. It publishes specifications; it does not ship a runtime. runC was *donated to* it [source: oci-overview-2026-08-23], which is a different relationship.\n569:This is the fiddliest material in the chapter and the highest value per minute of anything in it. The rules are small, entirely conditional, and almost nobody guesses the defaults correctly.\n603:The `Always` behavior also repays a careful reading, because its name oversells it. `Always` does not mean \"always download.\" It means always *check*: resolve the name to a digest at the registry, and if the local cache already holds that exact digest, use the cached copy [source: k8s-docs-images-2026-08-23]. Always re-resolve; download only on a miss. This is a favorite distractor, and now you know why the distractor is wrong.\n931:> **A** is wrong and is the single most consequential misreading: Kubernetes defines the interface and ships no runtime. **C** and **D** are both OCI concerns, `image-spec` and `distribution-spec` respectively [source: oci-overview-2026-08-23], which is the conflation §5's hazard callout addresses.\n\n=== frequency claims ===\n(none — good)","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9a1a6e6c-5296-4387-8e75-3543390421fa","uuid":"61077bdd-a890-42f2-9e8e-9100324d3d82","timestamp":"2026-08-24T05:44:57.074Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"=== superlative misconception claims ===\n338:- **A is wrong**, and it is the single most common misconception in this chapter: an image bundles application and system libraries, not a kernel [source: k8s-docs-containers-2026-08-23].\n348:- **A is wrong** for exactly that reason. This is the prior most readers arrive with.\n539:- **B is wrong**, and it is the most tempting distractor. The kubelet *ensures* that the containers described in PodSpecs are running and healthy [source: k8s-docs-cluster-architecture-2026-08-23]. It is the component that wants them to exist, not the one that creates them. It reaches a runtime across the CRI to do that.\n543:- **A is wrong**, and this is the most common misconception about the OCI. It publishes specifications; it does not ship a runtime. runC was *donated to* it [source: oci-overview-2026-08-23], which is a different relationship.\n569:This is the fiddliest material in the chapter and the highest value per minute of anything in it. The rules are small, entirely conditional, and almost nobody guesses the defaults correctly.\n603:The `Always` behavior also repays a careful reading, because its name oversells it. `Always` does not mean \"always download.\" It means always *check*: resolve the name to a digest at the registry, and if the local cache already holds that exact digest, use the cached copy [source: k8s-docs-images-2026-08-23]. Always re-resolve; download only on a miss. This is a favorite distractor, and now you know why the distractor is wrong.\n931:> **A** is wrong and is the single most consequential misreading: Kubernetes defines the interface and ships no runtime. **C** and **D** are both OCI concerns, `image-spec` and `distribution-spec` respectively [source: oci-overview-2026-08-23], which is the conflation §5's hazard callout addresses.\n\n=== frequency claims ===\n(none — good)","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
